     "page": 1,
     "text": "Scott and Cardenas Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Jennifer Saunders in consultation on November 09, 2025. \n\nRegarding her eating disorder, which she has successfully managed since its onset in April 2014, she remains currently controlled. She has not been prescribed any medications for this condition. \n\nHer aggressive NHL cancer, treated approximately 10 years ago, is also currently controlled with no need for ongoing medication. \n\nJennifer has a history of vitamin D deficiency diagnosed in August 2016, which she is managing with ergocalciferol 50000 IU. Her most recent lab results indicate that this condition is well-controlled.\n\nHer hypothyroidism, which began in November 2017, is currently controlled with levothyroxine 100 mcg. \n\nJennifer also suffers from seasonal allergies, first diagnosed in May 2022, which she manages with fluticasone nasal 50 mcg and loratadine mg. Her allergy symptoms remain controlled.\n\nFurthermore, Jennifer experienced a urinary tract infection in May 2019, which she successfully treated with a combination of sulfamethoxazole-trimethoprim 800/160 mg and nitrofurantoin 100 mg. This condition is currently controlled.\n\nIt is worth noting that Jennifer has been non-compliant with her medications and missed follow-up appointments on two occasions.\n\nSocially, Jennifer used to smoke cigarettes at a rate of 10 per day until she quit in July 2024. She currently consumes approximately one alcoholic drink per week.\n\nImpression and recommendations as above. Thank you for this referral.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Ashley Young\n"
    }
