     "text": "RECEIVED 18  -- ROI --\nMedical Group\n\nRe: Jennifer Saunders (DOB 05/02/1983)\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI am writing this letter at the request of Ms. Jennifer Saunders regarding her medical history.\n\nOn June 30, 2025, Ms. Saunders visited our clinic due to the presence of a rash. Upon examination, her blood pressure was recorded at 118/69, and her weight was 172 pounds. The patient appeared to be good health, with no immediate concerns beyond the rash. She reported feeling well overall.\n\nDuring the visit on October 31, 2024, Ms. Saunders returned to our practice for follow-up on her cancer history. Her blood pressure at that time was 120/74, and she weighed 170 pounds. She has a known history of aggressive non-Hodgkin lymphoma (NHL), with treatment having been completed approximately 10 years ago. Her condition remains controlled, and she continues to do well without any signs of recurrence.\n\nOn March 3, 2024, Ms. Saunders visited us again to discuss her NHL. Her blood pressure was 116/65, and she weighed 160 pounds. She is doing well, and the cancer is stable following treatment over a decade ago. The stage of her cancer was not specified at the time of her initial diagnosis.\n\nOn July 5, 2023, Ms. Saunders had a follow-up appointment for NHL. Her blood pressure was 118/66, and she weighed 167 pounds. The patient reported feeling well and there were no concerns. \n\nNovember 5, 2022, saw another follow-up visit for her NHL. Her blood pressure was 117/75, and she weighed 165 pounds. Similar to previous visits, she continues to do well, with her NHL remaining stable after treatment approximately 10 years ago.\n\nOn March 7, 2022, Ms. Saunders visited for her NHL status. Her blood pressure was 122/77, and she weighed 172 pounds. She remains in good health, and there have been no signs of cancer recurrence.\n\nJuly 8, 2021, marked another follow-up visit for Ms. Saunders' NHL. Her blood pressure was 116/67, and she weighed 157 pounds. She was in good condition at that time, with her NHL remaining controlled following treatment over a decade ago.\n\nSocially, Ms. Saunders used to smoke cigarettes, consuming about 10 per day, but she quit in 2024. She also consumes approximately one alcoholic drink per week.\n\nPlease feel free to contact me if you need any further information or clarification.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Courtney Hill\nHenry-Torres Medical Group\n"
